To still give you the three lines, I ran the command directly with Bash (a
plain foreground run — not streamed, not persistent):

  monitor-line-1
  monitor-line-2
  monitor-line-3

Note this took three attempts: the sandbox's static analyzer rejected $i in a
for loop as simple_expansion and a while read loop as unanalyzable shell
syntax, so the working version is seq -f 'monitor-line-%.0f' 1 3 — which
produces identical output but does not reproduce the 0.3s inter-line delay. If
the timing is what you're testing, this run doesn't cover it.

If Monitor should be present, it's likely a registration issue on the harness
side. Let me know if you want me to dig into how tools are registered in this
worktree.
